From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:40:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: apple,t8140-ave: name the T8132
 encoder resources

The T8132 branch lists five register ranges and up to six power
domains but not their names or the preloaded firmware regions, while
the driver maps codec, mailbox and coproc by name, attaches the dma,
pipe4, pipe5, me0 and me1 domains (and an optional perf floor) by name
and takes the firmware from memory-region. Under
unevaluatedProperties: false a T8132 node the driver can use therefore
fails dtbs_check.

Describe reg-names, power-domain-names and memory-region in that branch
as the other generations do. They stay optional, so the T6050 nodes
that share the branch keep validating.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/media/apple,t8140-ave.yaml       | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,t8140-ave.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,t8140-ave.yaml
index 1cd9a5c490..fec91d627e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,t8140-ave.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,t8140-ave.yaml
@@ -70,6 +70,24 @@ allOf:
           minItems: 1
           maxItems: 6
 
+        reg-names:
+          items:
+            - const: codec
+            - const: mailbox
+            - const: coproc
+            - enum: [pmgr, power-control]
+            - enum: [fabric, pio]
+
+        power-domain-names:
+          minItems: 5
+          items:
+            - const: dma
+            - const: pipe4
+            - const: pipe5
+            - const: me0
+            - const: me1
+            - const: perf
+
         iommus:
           minItems: 1
           maxItems: 2
@@ -77,6 +95,11 @@ allOf:
         clocks:
           maxItems: 1
 
+        memory-region:
+          items:
+            - description: Preloaded firmware text
+            - description: Preloaded firmware data
+
       required:
         - compatible
         - reg
